    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2AerpZARjPmAEDrDXc7FYpk)_\n\n## What\n- Emacs printed `Fetch dir data failed with error: (end-of-file)` at startup.\n\n## Cause\n- The message comes from Dirvish (`dirvish--dir-data-async`), not from an Info `dir` file.\n- `tabspaces` restores the saved session at startup, including a dired buffer (`~/Documents/writing/thesis/chapters/` in `var/tabspaces-session.eld`).\n- That opens a Dirvish buffer while Emacs is still starting, and its background directory scan returns nothing.\n\n## Fix\n- Register the `dired` buffer kind in `sp-tabs` with `#'ignore` for save and restore.\n- Dired buffers are no longer saved, and old dired records in the session file are skipped.\n- Same change in `docs/tangles/ui/sp-tabs.org` (new section with bullets).\n\n## Not tested\n- Emacs cannot boot the real config in the cloud container.\n- Not confirmed that the child process is killed mid-run rather than failing; this fix removes the trigger either way.\n- Branch is not number-prefixed (rename is blocked here); no `CHANGELOG.org` edit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBrcNzYWuC6MnPzHEG)_",
